#. [scenario]: id=01_Defend_the_Forest
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:13
msgid "Defend the Forest"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:26
msgid "The arrival of humans and orcs caused turmoil among the nations of the Great Continent. Elves, previously in uneasy balance with dwarves and others, had for centuries fought nothing more than an occasional skirmish. They were to find themselves facing conflicts of a long-forgotten intensity."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:30
msgid "Their first encounter with the newcomers went less well than either side might have wished."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:34
msgid "But humans, though crude and brash, at least had in them a creative spark which elves could recognize as akin to their own nature. Orcs seemed completely alien."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:38
msgid "For some years after Haldric’s people landed, orcs remained scarce more than a rumor to trouble the green fastnesses of the elves. That remained so until the day that an elvish noble of ancient line, Erlornas by name, faced an enemy unlike any he had ever met before."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#. "northern marches" is *not* a typo for "northern marshes" here.
#. In archaic English, "march" means "border country".
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:44
msgid "The orcs were first sighted from the north marches of the great forest of Wesmere."
msgstr ""

#. [side]: type=Orcish Warrior, id=Urugha
#. [side]: type=Orcish Slayer, id=Gharlsa
#. [side]: type=Orcish Warlord, id=Gnargha
#. [side]: type={TYPE}
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:69
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:77
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:59
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:77
msgid "Orcs"
msgstr ""

#. [side]: type=Orcish Warrior, id=Urugha
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:74
msgid "Urugha"
msgstr ""

#. [unit]: type=Elvish Rider, id=Lomarfel
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:94
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:387
msgid "Lomarfel"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Lomarfel
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:112
msgid "My lord! A party of aliens has made camp to the north and lays waste to the forest. Our scouts believe it’s a band of orcs."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:116
msgid "Orcs? It seems unlikely. The human king, Haldric, crushed them when they landed on these shores, and since then they’ve been no more than a bogey mothers use to scare the children."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Lomarfel
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:120
msgid "So it seemed, my lord. Yet there is a band of them in the north cutting down healthy trees by the dozen, and making great fires from the wood. They trample the greensward into mud and do not even bury their foul dung. I believe I can smell the stench even here."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:124
msgid "So the grim tales of them prove true. They must not be allowed to continue; we must banish this blight from our forests. I shall marshal the wardens and drive them off. And the Council needs to hear of this; take the message and return with reinforcements, for there might be more of them."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Lomarfel
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:128
msgid "Yes, my lord!"
msgstr ""

#. [objective]: condition=win
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:146
msgid "Defeat Urugha"
msgstr ""

#. [objective]: condition=lose
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:150
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:214
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:349
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:180
msgid "Death of Erlornas"
msgstr ""

#. [note]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:160
msgid "Elves can move quickly and safely among the trees. Pick off the enemy grunts with your archers from the safety of the forest."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:173
msgid "Look at them. Big, slow, clumsy and hardly a bow in hand. Keep to the trees, use your arrows and the day will be ours."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: race=elf
#. the player hasn't recruited any Shamans. This message isn't shown if they have a Shaman, even if she has 0 xp.
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:222
msgid "My lord, none of our healers have experience on the battlefield. It pleases me that they are safe, but if we should embark on a campaign then we will surely need them alongside us in the battles ahead."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: race=elf
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:223
msgid "female^My lord, none of our healers have experience on the battlefield. It pleases me that they are safe, but if we should embark on a campaign then we will surely need them alongside us in the battles ahead."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: race=elf
#. the player has recruited some Shamans but has lost all them (or managed to level a Sorceress)
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:237
msgid "My lord, none of our surviving healers have experience on the battlefield. It pains me to suggest that we should risk another, but if we should embark on a campaign then we will surely need them alongside us in the battles ahead."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: race=elf
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:238
msgid "female^My lord, none of our surviving healers have experience on the battlefield. It pains me to suggest that we should risk another, but if we should embark on a campaign then we will surely need them alongside us in the battles ahead."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=unit
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:269
msgid "I’ve been bested, but the combat wasn’t fair... A thousand curses on you, withered coward! May you suffer... and when my master, Rualsha, finds you may he wipe your people from the face of this earth!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:276
msgid "Rualsha? Hmm... What if... Assemble a war-party, we need to scout north!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#. role=advisor will always be a male unit of the Elvish Scout line.
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:296
msgid "It’s hopeless; we’ve tried everything, and they’re still coming back."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Urugha
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:300
msgid "Forward, you worthless worms! Look at them, they’re tired and afraid! You killed their will to fight, now go and finish the job!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:304
msgid "That cloud of dust on the horizon... flee! There’s more of the abominations heading this way! Fall back before we’re outnumbered and crushed."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:309
msgid "Lord Erlornas didn’t drive the orcs back, although he and his warriors tried their absolute best. When another war band arrived, elvish resistance crumbled."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/01_Defend_the_Forest.cfg:314
msgid "Of the ensuing events little is known, since much was lost in the chaos and confusion, but one thing is painfully sure. Elves lost the campaign."
msgstr ""

#. [scenario]: id=02_Wasteland
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:23
msgid "Wasteland"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:38
msgid "The path of the orcish war band was easy to follow — a wide swathe of trampled ground through violated forest. Erlornas and his party swiftly followed it north and west."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:42
msgid "As they fared further north the green forest thinned around them, slowly fading into a barren and fallow country. The signs were obvious and unmistakable — tree stumps, an occasional half-rotten tree felled long ago, and dead wood around them in scarce grass. This had been forest once, like the woods they called home. It had been murdered."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:46
msgid "There was no trail to be found here; wind and rain had erased the spoor. Fortunately, there was no need of a trail; smoke on the horizon betrayed the presence of their enemies."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:50
msgid "Erlornas was near-certain they would find orcs there. No clan of dwarves would break their ancient treaties with the elves in this way; humans were never so...methodical in their destruction, and did not travel in sufficiently large numbers in a north country they found too cold and damp for comfort. The great question remained — would he find Rualsha?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:54
msgid "Perhaps, but not here. The tribe this camp housed was too small to impress fear on other orcs. Come next morning, the elves were prepared for battle."
msgstr ""

#. [side]: type=Orcish Slayer, id=Gharlsa
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:82
msgid "Gharlsa"
msgstr ""

#. [side]: type=Orcish Warrior, id=Krughnar
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:108
msgid "Rival Orcs"
msgstr ""

#. [side]: type=Orcish Warrior, id=Krughnar
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:113
msgid "Krughnar"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:174
msgid "The trail leads straight to this place, my lord."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:178
msgid "There is a keep ahead of us. How comes it that we know nothing of it? I thought our borders were watched more carefully."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:182
msgid "I... I know not, my lord. For ages there was no one in these lands that could build such a thing save us. I fear we have fallen prey a false sense of security that has injured the vigilance of our scouts."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:186
msgid "When the fighting ends, I’ll have some answers. But for now—"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Gharlsa
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:190
msgid "Gharlsa sees elves... yes... Fresh meat for wolves. Yes, yes..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:194
msgid "— let’s focus on the task at hand."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:198
msgid "Does that demented creature truly believe he can kill us?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:202
msgid "Appearances can be deceiving. Tell the men to be cautious."
msgstr ""

#. [objective]: condition=win
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:210
msgid "Defeat Gharlsa"
msgstr ""

#. [note]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:224
msgid "Assassins are hard to hit, and their poison is insidious. Stay close to the villages, where poisoning can be cured, and force your enemies to attack you from the river."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Krughnar
#. Krughnar is a follower of Lich-Lord Selmar. He calls the other orcs traitors because they've rebelled, and follow Rualsha instead. The player doesn't know this yet.
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:310
msgid "I have caught you at last, traitorous Gharlsa! May your spirit suffer greatly for your weakness!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Gharlsa
#. Gharlsa is a follower of Rualsha, another orc - not the Lich-Lord Selmar that Krughnar follows. The player doesn't know this yet.
#. "orcs only obey orcs" is also a similar theme to what Rualsha says in the final scenario
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:316
msgid "Traitor? No... you betray. Gharlsa only obey orcs. Rualsha great orc. Yes, yes... Rualsha true leader."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Krughnar
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:320
msgid "Rise up, grunts! We have a great fight upon us! Let your rage flow freely! Let your blades slay all! First one to draw blood will feast by my fire this night!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:333
msgid "It seems this “Rualsha’s” leadership does not stand uncontested. The orcs have turned their attention from us to their rival. The two camps mean to destroy each other, and much of our forest in the process."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:337
msgid "Aim true, men, with wit and courage the day will be ours. And spare no-one, there can be no orc south of the hills, else we’ll never have peace again."
msgstr ""

#. [objective]: condition=win
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:345
msgid "Defeat both enemy leaders"
msgstr ""

#. [note]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:359
msgid "Your enemies are focused on each other. Gather gold and build your army while they exhaust their armies, then move in and finish them off."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Gharlsa
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:379
msgid "Yes... yes... Slay them!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=unit
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:396
msgid "Hurts... failed... Rualsha gonna be angry..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=unit
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:412
msgid "You won... Elf... But it changes... Nothing... (*cough*)"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=unit
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:416
msgid "We found the way... Now... We will come in numbers... (*cough*) You can’t imagine..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=unit
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:420
msgid "(*cough*) I’ll be waiting... Among the dead..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:452
msgid "The orcish chieftain finally fell, overcome by his wounds. The elves found themselves in a half-ruined camp littered with the bodies of both sides, there was no hale orc in sight, nor did any of the wounded beg mercy. The elves took no prisoners."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:461
msgid "It’s done, lord. No-one escaped. No-one tried to escape. I’m... disturbed."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:465
msgid "Good. But their disregard for self-preservation is astounding. As is their ferocity when defending what they claim as their own. Have the scouts found others this side of the hills?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:469
msgid "No, lord. But trolls were spotted in the hills ahead. Do we really need to cross them to the north?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:473
msgid "Yes. The council has spoken to me through a dream-sending. They are troubled. Reinforcements have been sent after us, but we need to press on. Tell the men to rest, we’ll move out at dawn."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:491
msgid "We can’t carry on, lord, the men are too tired. We have to fall back."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:495
msgid "Damn it. Sound the retreat, we’ll try again when reinforcements arrive."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/02_Wasteland.cfg:500
msgid "The expected relief caught up with them a few days later. The following morning they took the field against a far larger host of orcs. The battle ended in a draw; the war raged on for years..."
msgstr ""

#. [scenario]: id=03_Valley_of_Trolls
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:22
msgid "Valley of Trolls"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:36
msgid "Next morning, the elves set off again, increasingly wearied by the hardships of the campaign and longing for the green comfort of their home forests. This land was barren and rugged; nothing shielded them from biting northern wind as they traveled towards the mountains looming before them."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:40
msgid "At dusk they arrived at the mouth of a valley cutting almost straight through the range and made camp, as scouts warned that the area was hostile and the road ahead treacherous in darkness. There were no songs or music that night and most of the elves slept uneasily. An unlucky few kept a cautious watch."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:44
msgid "When sunrise came, the elves moved into battle formations. Whatever waited in the slopes ahead, it would not find them unprepared."
msgstr ""

#. [side]: type={TYPE}
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:68
msgid "Trolls"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:135
msgid "We are far from our lands, now, Erlornas, and we have driven the orcs from the forest. Why do we not return home?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:139
msgid "You know well enough... Rualsha. That name sounds everywhere we go since the incursion began. That orc is much more than a mere marauding bandit in search of pillage. And he wants this land. <i>Our</i> land. He is planning an invasion, I’m sure of it. We must gather more information about his plans before we go back."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:143
msgid "And tell me... How did you sleep last night?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:147
msgid "How did I?... Uneasy, lord. My dreams were bleak, some of them nightmares."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:151
msgid "Yes. The earth currents are perturbed here, and the bridges to the dreamland are tainted. I think there is a mage dwelling somewhere nearby. Or perhaps more than one; the traces are mixed, and some of them have an unwholesome flavor."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:155
msgid "It would be dire indeed for us if these orcs have magic to add to their battle-might."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:159
msgid "We must discover if this is so."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:163
msgid "Information will do us no good if we are killed before we return with it! These mountains look like troll territory."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:167
msgid "Enough. The sun’s fully over the horizon. Give the order to advance."
msgstr ""

#. [objective]: condition=win
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:176
msgid "Move Erlornas to the west edge of the map"
msgstr ""

#. [note]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:190
msgid "Trolls are poor fighters when not on rugged terrain and fare even worse during the daytime. Lure them out of the hills and attack in the sunlight."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=unit
#. [message]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:207
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:257
msgid "Dis not over! Rualsha gonna make you pay!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:211
msgid "The chieftain blocking the pass is slain, lord. The way forward is clear."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:244
msgid "I have fought my way through. Break camp and move everyone through the pass before they rally. We’ll rest a bit on the other side; we have earned it."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:248
msgid "At once. How much time do you think we have?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:252
msgid "A day, perhaps. We fought three clans today; they won’t take long to rally. We need to be gone from here by sunset next."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:274
msgid "We can’t get through, my lord. These whelps are not individually very dangerous, but there are huge numbers of them."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:278
msgid "Four days of combat and nothing to show for it. How does it feel to you?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:282
msgid "Terrible, my lord. Never in my life did I dream I’d be bested by mere trolls. What are your orders?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:286
msgid "Withdraw and make camp a safe distance from the hills. There is no further point in this fight. We’ll wait for reinforcements."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:291
msgid "The reinforcements arrived a few days later, a crack force of rangers with some cavalry support. When they attempted the pass again, they found not trolls but something worse — an orcish army approaching from the north."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/03_Valley_of_Trolls.cfg:296
msgid "The battle that ensued was bloody and inconclusive, and the elven losses were only the beginning of the mournful toll in a war that would rage for many years after."
msgstr ""

#. [scenario]: id=04_Linaera_the_Quick
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:13
msgid "Linaera the Quick"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:27
msgid "After a day of hard-earned rest the elves marched north again. This was unknown country, not frequented even by Wesmere’s furthermost-faring scouts."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:31
msgid "Two days’ travel later, the forward scouts reported another orcish warband laying siege to a tower."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:35
msgid "Erlornas surveyed the siege from atop a small tree-covered hill overlooking the tower valley..."
msgstr ""

#. [side]: type=Orcish Warlord, id=Gnargha
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:64
msgid "Gnargha"
msgstr ""

#. [side]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:98
msgid "Mages"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:167
msgid "Report."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:173
msgid "A warband of orcs, no women or children among them, besieges a tower. It’s of human design... but we are far from the lands granted to humans by treaty, my lord Erlornas."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:177
msgid "Under the letter of the treaty, it is so. But this country is too cold and barren for us. I wonder, what manner of human would choose to live here, far from its kind? Hmmm..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:181
msgid "It trespasses, and should be driven out!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:185
msgid "Hold. It is only one human, or a few of them at most. Time enough to speak of driving it out when we have no enemies in common."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:189
msgid "Tell me: I see no bridge over the chasm around that keep. Is there any sign that one has been withdrawn by the defenders?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:193
msgid "No, lord. No traces of any construction. It looks like no bridge has ever existed there. There must be other, hidden means of access to the tower."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:198
msgid "Interesting... Go to my personal stores and bring me a bottle of wine. And a couple of glasses."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:203
msgid "... Glasses?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:207
msgid "Do it. We’ll have a guest soon."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#. "Faerie" in this paragraph is a rare, poetic word in
#. English. It is the proper name of a magical otherworld
#. associated with elves - actually, originally with
#. fairies, but before Tolkien the boundary between elves
#. and fairies was extremely blurry. In Wesnoth it is
#. deliberately unclear whether Faerie is a place that is
#. the source of magical power or a label for the inner
#. nonhuman/magical nature of the Elves. Translate freely.
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:222
msgid "Erlornas closed his eyes and brought his hands forward, joined palms forming a cup open to the sky. Soon they began to glow, then to flare like a brazier with the fire of Faerie, casting a cold, blue light all around the elf-lord. A wisp of light emerged from the eerie flames, and at a few murmured words from the elf-lord flew away towards the tower below. Then the light around Erlornas faded and all was seemingly as before."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:226
msgid "Some time later..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:250
msgid "So you decided to accept the invitation. Good. Welcome, I am Lord Erlornas of Wesmere. I find your presence here... surprising."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:254
msgid "Scarcely less than I find yours, my lord elf, but I would welcome your aid against these orcs. They have been besieging my tower for weeks. I dare not flee lest they chase me down."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:258
msgid "I wish their foul kind driven as far as possible from my borders, not to return. But you will explain your presence here before petitioning my aid. These lands are not of those that were appointed to man."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#. "some import" (import having identical meaning as"importance") is under-selling it; a Lich-Lord is a very serious danger.
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:263
msgid "My apprentices and I have come to reconnoiter, regarding a danger of some import. Perhaps you have sensed it too; black magic is in the air. A Lich-Lord of the Green Isle holds dominion in these lands."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#. The speaker is an elf, referring to a human king as "man-king" in the same way that a human might refer to an elf as an "elf-king".
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:268
msgid "Preposterous. Lich-Lord Jevyan perished close to a decade ago, at the hands of your man-king."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#. This is Lich-Lord Selmar from WoF.
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:273
msgid "This one calls himself Selmar. In his lair, he has opened a great stone gate to the heart of the homeland of the orcs in the distant west. I probed the gateway from afar for many days, before these orcs beheld me and pursued me."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#. "those whose flesh can cross a chasm as easily as can a thought cross the mind" is a poetic way of referring to Linaera's teleportation.
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:278
msgid "More than probed, I see you have gleaned from its secrets. Few are those whose flesh can cross a chasm as easily as can a thought cross the mind."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:282
msgid "Silver magic — now I understand. So this is how these orcs have returned to trouble us. If what you speak is true, I am certain the Council would agree: this Lich-Lord must be slain and his portal quenched."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:286
msgid "And what of Rualsha? The spectre of that name has haunted us ever since our first encounter with these beasts."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:290
msgid "That seems an orcish name, but I do not know its owner. I have been trapped here for weeks, unable to reconnoiter nor report home."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:294
msgid "Very well. Your petition for aid is granted, Linaera of the folk of Haldric. Count me as an ally and we will defeat this threat together, beginning here."
msgstr ""

#. [object]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:302
msgid "New Recruits"
msgstr ""

#. [object]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:303
msgid "You can now recruit Mages."
msgstr ""

#. [object]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:304
msgid "Both Erlornas and Linaera can recruit and recall when standing on a keep."
msgstr ""

#. [objective]: condition=win
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:313
msgid "Defeat Gnargha"
msgstr ""

#. [objective]: condition=lose
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:317
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:228
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:467
msgid "Death of Erlornas or Linaera"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:368
msgid "And that is well ended. I stand in your debt, Erlornas of Wesmere."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#. "a threeday’s march" isn't a real word, but is an archaic-sounding way to say "three days’ march
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:373
msgid "Indeed. But the greater threat remains; now I, too, sense the taint of this orc-gate, scarce a threeday’s march away. We must go swiftly, across the fields."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:377
msgid "I should advise against it, lord elf. Orcs have wholly taken these lands, swarming in great numbers over the plains and the hills. Traveling openly, you will surely find yourself hunted."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:381
msgid "We have warred with orcs before, madame mage."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#. "skirmished" is in contrast to the previous line's "warred". A skirmish is much smaller in scale. Erlorans is saying they aren't prepared to fight huge bands of orcs.
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:386
msgid "We have <i>skirmished</i> with orcs. I should not be so quick to pit our merry little band against all the vastness of the north. What counsel do you tender, Linaera?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:390
msgid "Near to us is a swamp, which extends some distance towards our goal. Evil things have made a nest there; foul creatures born of the lich. But orcs stay out of it, and there are firm paths on which to tread."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/04_Linaera_the_Quick.cfg:394
msgid "Very well. Support from Wesmere follows close in my wake, but we cannot wait. I entrust your tower-keeper with my seal, and with directions for my kin. We make for the swamp."
msgstr ""

#. [scenario]: id=05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:13
msgid "A Detour through the Swamp"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:27
msgid "Leaving their wounded to mend within Linaera’s tower, the remaining elves and their human allies marched forth into the swamp. The rank stench of decay surrounded them while insects and vermin churned in the earth."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:31
msgid "The forward scouts soon reported signs of undead ahead. Erlornas moved the elves into battle formations."
msgstr ""

#. [side]: type={ON_DIFFICULTY4 Necrophage Ghast Ghast Ghast}, id=leader2
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:56
msgid "Undead"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:195
msgid "The evil spirits who have settled in this wetland have turned it into a vile bog. I crossed here twice before by stealth, yet... this time something is changed."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:202
msgid "Look! These undead are injured, decaying from neglect. Their lich master offers them no power. Where is the cruel will what first raised them from the ground?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:206
msgid "Lucky for us. We can reach our destination by the western way or the northern way, though neither will be without its perils. Destroying the undead leader should also suffice, although there is little need; it seems these ones will soon crumble of their own accord."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:210
msgid "Whichever path we take, we must be sure to prepare ourselves for the final battle ahead. I fear we shall have need of all the gold and experience we can gather ere we come to the gate."
msgstr ""

#. [objective]: condition=win
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:219
msgid "Move Erlornas to the north edge of the map"
msgstr ""

#. [objective]: condition=win
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:224
msgid "Defeat the enemy leader"
msgstr ""

#. [note]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:238
msgid "Ghosts are resistant to physical attack. Use Mages to attack ghosts, and elves to protect and support the Mages."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=unit
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:290
msgid "Here is the corpse of an orc. He was felled perhaps two weeks ago, and by a blade of his own kind’s make. Many more bodies lie deeper in the swamp."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:294
msgid "The bodies also reek of dark magic, and the craters on this blasted land bear witness to countless spells. I think orcs fought a great battle here, against other orcs and undead. A battle for control of the gate, perhaps?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:298
msgid "This swamp is not far from your tower. Should your magical senses not have noticed this sooner?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:302
msgid "To my inner eye the orc-gate is as a blazing inferno, bright enough to be blinding. In comparison even a mighty blast of lightning would be but a matchstick, and difficult to notice if I were not watching for it."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:306
msgid "But now that I know what to look for, I feel similar magical scars all around these lands. Whatever battle this was, this swamp is not the only place it was fought. A mystery, but it bodes well for us — if there has been fighting near the gate, its defenses may already be weakened."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=unit
#. Said by the enemy leader (a Ghast) as it dies.
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:337
msgid "..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:372
msgid "The end of our road lies close before us. Both the lich and its fell gate must be brought to ruin. The one may be done by blade, but the other is a thing wholly unknown to my folk."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:376
msgid "Limited, personal teleportation notwithstanding, I grasp only the barest fragments of the gateway’s working. In truth, I suspect all the sages of man might study it for a dozen years and yet not fathom its creation."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:380
msgid "But to answer your implied question: yes, I possess sufficient knowledge to undo this creation of the Lich-Lords. We must first destroy the lich, as I will require his body in order to dispel his magic."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:384
msgid "You know a great deal of Lich-Lords, Linaera of the folk of Haldric. Yet you say you have studied this portal only from afar, and for but some few days?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#. Linaera is one of the Wesfolk, and formerly lived in Jevyan's Haven. After the events of TRoW the Wesfolk have joined with Haldric to found the nation of Wesnoth.
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:389
msgid "I mingle with the men of Haldric, lord elf, but I am not counted among their number. I am Wesfolk. I studied under Jevyan and dwelt in his Haven, ere the betrayal. That is how I learned magery, and that is also why I and not another was sent on this mission."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:393
msgid "The works of this other Lich-Lord are newer to me. But with his bones, I am confident I can undo his gate. It is far easier to destroy than to create, lord elf; already you know this."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/05_A_Detour_through_the_Swamp.cfg:397
msgid "Indeed. The orcs know it as well, better than any among us; their senseless destruction is... overwhelming. I fear what doom awaits Wesmere should we fail. Let us press on."
msgstr ""

#. [scenario]: id=06_Showdown
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:30
msgid "Showdown"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:44
msgid "Marching hard through the night, the sore wearied elves emerged from the swamp onto an arid plain. They gazed in dismay at the wasteland, strewn with refuse, boot-prints, and the broken stumps of slaughtered trees. What plants still clung to the meagre soil were blasted by cold, sandy winds."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:48
msgid "Ahead, the very air hung heavy with enchantment. It grew hard to draw breath. Rumbles and tremors in the earth bore witness to the power the Lich-Lord had unleashed."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:52
msgid "The scouts soon spotted orcs ahead, only to find the creatures engaged in an unexpected work."
msgstr ""

#. [unit]: id=Rualsha, type=Orcish Sovereign
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:237
msgid "Rualsha"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Rualsha
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:310
msgid "—you dared resist Rualsha! You were led astray by the lich! But now you are beaten, and in defeat you see the truth. Do you swear fealty to me, and only me?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=leader5
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:314
msgid "Yes, High Orc!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=helper5
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:318
msgid "Yes, King Rualsha!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Rualsha
#. WoF mentions that Lich-Lord Selmar is interested in summoning giants from the Old Continent. Giants aren't a faction in Wesnoth and probably never will be, but this is a nod to that.
#. These orcs just came from the Old Continent, so if there are giants there, these orcs would know about them.
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:324
msgid "Never again will orc bow to man, nor giant, nor lord of bones. Orc will only bow to orc! And who is the greatest orc of all?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=helper5
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:328
msgid "You are, King Rualsha!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=leader5
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:334
msgid "My warriors obey only you!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:343
msgid "So you are Rualsha. At last we meet."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Rualsha
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:347
msgid "Raaahhh! Who dares interrupt me? Pointy ears... dainty wrists... snooty nose... you must be elves."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#. Rualsha is the "Orcish Sovereign" unit. This is a nod to that, but not crucial to keep in the translation.
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:352
msgid "Indeed. We elves have heard your name many times, sovereign. Yet I was unsure if I would find you here."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Rualsha
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:356
msgid "Ha! Am I not the gate-king you thought to meet? That wretched lich is dead, felled weeks ago by my hand. He brought me here to do his bidding, but in the end it was <b><i>I</i></b> who bested <b><i>him</i></b>."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Rualsha
#. the Orcish Sovereign's portrait includes a necklace of bones
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:361
msgid "Now his portal is mine; his bones my trophy! The last of his followers have sworn fealty to me, or else fallen under my blade!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:366
msgid "Rualsha wears some of the lich’s bones around his neck. I must have them to dispel the gate."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Rualsha
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:370
msgid "If you think to stop me, elf, you come too late. Thousands, hundreds of thousands of orcs have already spread across the north."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Rualsha
#. "your jewel" refers to the Ruby of Fire, which we know the orcs tried to take in LoW. But this campaign isn't about the ruby, so it's only an oblique reference.
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:375
msgid "The lich was weak; he dared command only a few of those who came, for fear of revolt. But I am strong, and I am orc; the hordes will gladly flock to my banner. Your jewel will be mine, your forests reduced to firewood, and your people left begging for a merciful death!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Lomarfel
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:400
msgid "My lord! What is this terrible place? We have ridden hard for over a week to catch up with you."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Lomarfel
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:429
msgid "I bring a weighty war-chest and the reinforcements you requested from the Ka’lian, Lord Erlornas. The council has deliberated, and sets in your hands full authority over this matter of the orcs."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#. $amount will be between 150 and 75
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:441
msgid "You have gained $amount gold!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:451
msgid "Fortunate is your hour of arrival, Lomarfel. I fear Rualsha’s host is too great for us to vanquish in open battle, even with your aid. But the Rangers who have come with you are skilled in stealth."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:455
msgid "Even in the blasted ruins of this place, they can still pass veiled from orcish gaze, and fall upon Rualsha from behind. Once the finishing blow is struck, we will seal his portal and bring this matter to an end."
msgstr ""

#. [objective]: condition=win
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:463
msgid "Defeat Rualsha"
msgstr ""

#. [note]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:472
msgid "Your enemy is well-defended against attacks from the south. Use rangers to sneak through the eastern forest and mount a surprise attack from the north."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=unit
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:671
msgid "Aarrggh!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Rualsha
#. A Sylph or a Shyde has just tried to fly through a magical portal, but units can only exit from the portal, not enter it. The Sylph/Shyde tok damage and was expelled from the portal. "flutter-rat" is a derogatory reference to their wings.
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:676
msgid "One way only, flutter-rat."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Rualsha
#. Rualsha has just been attacked by an army of elves
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:702
msgid "I will have your heads!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Rualsha
#. Rualsha has just been ambushed by elves hiding in forest
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:709
msgid "Treachery! I will have your heads!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=unit
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:734
msgid "You may slay me, Erlornas, but my people live on. They will not forget! They will pursue you, and destroy you utterly... we will... we... arrgh..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:746
msgid "Now is our chance, Linaera!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:779
msgid "The gate... I am overwhelmed by its power! To think that even Selmar, weakest of the Lich-Lords, could sculpt a creation of this magnificence."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:783
msgid "Hurry! Destroy the foul thing before yet more orcs emerge!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:787
msgid "So much Wesfolk knowledge has been lost, Erlornas. First in our flight from the Old Continent, then by our wars on the Green Isle and the deaths of our Lords. And now am I to destroy this, too: this final monument to the greatness of my once-proud people?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:791
msgid "Alas. Such is the price of our survival."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:800
msgid "As the orc drew his last ragged breath, the Wesfolk mage spoke a word and cast forth her hand..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:831
msgid "It is done."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:835
msgid "We have won! The orcish warbands will scatter! In time the sands shall drink deeply of their blood."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:839
msgid "Perhaps. But I fear Rualsha spake truth. So many have already come through the gate. If hundreds of thousands of orcs have already spread across the north, how are we ever to be rid of them?"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/scenarios/06_Showdown.cfg:843
msgid "Come, we must hasten from this place while the way is yet clear. We have won a first victory here, but I fear dark times will come upon its heels..."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Gateway, race=undead
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/units/Gateway.cfg:4
msgid "Gateway"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Gateway, race=undead
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/units/Gateway.cfg:22
msgid "A work of madness..."
msgstr ""

#. [side]
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/characters.cfg:20
msgid "Elves"
msgstr ""

#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/characters.cfg:50
msgid "Erlornas"
msgstr ""

#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/characters.cfg:64
msgid "Linaera"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/deaths.cfg:20
msgid "Ugh..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Urugha
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/deaths.cfg:24
msgid "Finally! Got him!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: race=elf
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/deaths.cfg:31
msgid "Lord!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/deaths.cfg:35
msgid "Take... command... Drive them... away."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/deaths.cfg:42
msgid "Lord Erlornas died the day he first fought the orcs and never saw the end of the war. Given its final outcome, this was perhaps for the best."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=second_unit
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/deaths.cfg:62
msgid "Ha! Me smashed da funny elf. Me got a trophy!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: role=advisor
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/deaths.cfg:66
msgid "No! This can’t be!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/deaths.cfg:71
msgid "Soon after Erlornas died, the elven party, lacking a leader and pressed from all sides, scattered and fled. Their retreat to Wesmere was arduous and long."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/deaths.cfg:75
msgid "During their retreat, the pass was crossed by another army moving in the opposite direction. Orcs were back south of the pass, and this time they were to stay for a long, long time."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/deaths.cfg:92
msgid "Lord Erlornas never saw the blade that felled him. He died on the spot, with not a chance to issue last commands or farewells. Without him his wardens soon fell into confusion, and losing heart withdrew from the battle."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=narrator
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/deaths.cfg:97
msgid "When reinforcements finally arrived, elves managed to dislodge the orcish tribe. But the threat from the north remained unresolved and loomed large over their future."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Linaera
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/deaths.cfg:117
msgid "Alas, Erlornas, I have failed us..."
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Erlornas
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/deaths.cfg:123
msgid "All is lost! Without Linaera’s help, I cannot hope to succeed!"
msgstr ""

#. [message]: speaker=Lomarfel
#: data/campaigns/An_Orcish_Incursion/utils/deaths.cfg:141
msgid "Erlornas, you must defeat Rualsha! I have given my all..."
msgstr ""

